:false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"There is an application that I developed based on the [kafka-quikstart](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-quickstarts/tree/master/kafka-quickstart) example. The application runs smoothly in my local and the messages coming to the topic I defined are gotten in the EventListener.\r\n\r\n```java\r\n@ApplicationScoped\r\npublic class EventListener\r\n{\r\n   @Inject\r\n   Logger logger;\r\n\r\n   @Incoming(\"turnover\")\r\n   @Outgoing(\"turnover-stream\")\r\n   @Broadcast\r\n   @Acknowledgment(Acknowledgment.Strategy.PRE_PROCESSING)\r\n   public TurnOverEvent process(TurnOverEvent event){\r\n      logger.info(\"Incoming event is {}\", event);\r\n      return event;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\nBut I see that the code not working when I deployed the native jar on the cloud platform. In my Kafka cluster, messages delivered to the relevant topic are not gotten by the application. \r\n\r\nWhereas, I see the channel successfully connected to the topic when I examine the pods logs \r\n\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,634 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.provider] (main) SRMSG00208: Deployment done... start processing\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,635 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.provider] (main) SRMSG00226: Found incoming connectors: [smallrye-kafka]\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,635 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.provider] (main) SRMSG00227: Found outgoing connectors: [smallrye-kafka]\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,635 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.provider] (main) SRMSG00229: Channel manager initializing...\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,637 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.kafka] (main) SRMSG18200: Merging config with {bootstrap.servers=172.16.1.5:9091,172.16.1.5:9092,172.16.1.5:9093}\r\n> 2020-09-16 15:59:15,638 INFO  [io.sma.rea.mes.kafka] (main) SRMSG18229: Consumed topics for channel 'turnover': [avixTurnOverEventTopic]\r\n> 213095 INFO org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ConsumerConfig  main - ConsumerConfig values:\r\n> \tallow.auto.create.topics = true\r\n> \tauto.commit.interval.ms